1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,560
Before we left, I closed my eyes

2
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:06,854
and tried to remember what
a clear blue sky looked like...

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,340
When factories and fires pumped sulfur
and nitrogen gases into the air,

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,831
they mixed with water droplets
in the clouds to create acid rain:

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,215
polluted rain that damaged
forests, poisoned lakes,

6
00:00:19,295 --> 00:00:21,601
and ruined the soil where our food grew.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,179
[MISSION CONTROL]
All systems locked.

8
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,905
Oxygen reserves nominal.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,740
Main engine ignition in...

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:31,920
3...

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:32,920
3... 2...

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:33,920
3... 2... 1...

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,275
Liftoff.

14
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:38,320
We didn't leave Earth
because we wanted to explore.

15
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,639
We left because we broke
our own life-support system.

16
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,705
As our rocket climbed past the clouds,

17
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:50,492
we broke through the thick layer of smoke
and aerosols trapping the heat below.

18
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:54,875
Looking down from orbit,

19
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:58,890
Earth didn't look like the "Blue Marble"
from old NASA photos anymore...

20
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,346
it was wrapped in a hazy gray blanket.

21
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,400
Earth gave us air, water, food,

22
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:08,770
and protection from space
radiation for free...

23
00:01:09,050 --> 00:01:10,757
and we took it for granted.

24
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,310
Now, on Mars, we have
to build every breath of air

25
00:01:14,390 --> 00:01:16,806
and every drop of water ourselves...

26
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,855
hoping that one day,
Earth's sky will clear,

27
00:01:19,935 --> 00:01:21,760
and we'll know how to protect it.

